    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0509" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 851.857Su8/23</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-04T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1916, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3141. Please ascertain definitely whether the <hi rendition="#italic">Sussex</hi>
                    was ever used by the British Government as a transport or troopship and whether
                    the route followed by transports is the same as that followed by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sussex</hi> on her last trip.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
